(7516581, 1200354, 67258, '<td valign="top">Back to clarify my comment, especially in light of Ubique''s.  I love every aspect of this, except at the very bottom of the frame where the tree appears to grow out of the giraffe.  I really like the inclusion of the rest of it (and I concede it would look pretty silly without the bottom..) and love the way the giraffe''s head appears above the leaves.  I hadn''t consciously considered that the foreground tree/bush, acted as an echo of the form of the animal, but I appreciate the photo all the more for having that connection pointed out.  Edit: Deserved a much higher finish tan this<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2017-06-02 01:25:39.</i></td>', 'Back to clarify my comment, especially in light of Ubique''s.  I love every aspect of this, except at the very bottom of the frame where the tree appears to grow out of the giraffe.  I really like the inclusion of the rest of it (and I concede it would look pretty silly without the bottom..) and love the way the giraffe''s head appears above the leaves.  I hadn''t consciously considered that the foreground tree/bush, acted as an echo of the form of the animal, but I appreciate the photo all the more for having that connection pointed out.  Edit: Deserved a much higher finish tan this', '2017-06-02 02:24:59.000000', '2017-06-02 02:25:39.000000', 0),
